Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the columns that matter for the question, together with the role each one will probably play and some typical filter conditions that may be useful.

Relevant columns and their potential usage
• olist_order_items.order_id: join bridge between items and payments.  
• olist_order_items.product_id: join bridge between items and products.  
• olist_products.product_category_name: product‑level category we finally want to rank.  
• product_category_name_translation.product_category_name_english: readable English category (optional).  
• olist_order_payments.order_id: join bridge between payments and items (→ products).  
• olist_order_payments.payment_type: the payment type that must be counted.  
• olist_order_payments.payment_value: could be aggregated but is NOT required here – we only need counts.

Typical conditions you might see
• olist_products.product_category_name IS NOT NULL  
• olist_order_payments.payment_type IS NOT NULL  
• JOIN … ON oi.order_id = op.order_id  
• JOIN … ON oi.product_id = p.product_id  
• Possibly LEFT JOIN product_category_name_translation ON translation.product_category_name = p.product_category_name  

10 exploratory‑to‑solution SQL queries  
(Each query is limited to 20 rows to keep the exploratory result sets small.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Look at the different payment types that exist.
SELECT DISTINCT payment_type
FROM olist_order_payments
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Quick ranking of payment types by overall number of payments.
SELECT payment_type,
       COUNT(*) AS num_payments
FROM   olist_order_payments
GROUP  BY payment_type
ORDER  BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Inspect how items connect to products (category visible).
SELECT oi.order_id,
       oi.product_id,
       p.product_category_name
FROM   olist_order_items AS oi
JOIN   olist_products     AS p ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Distinct list of product categories that are present.
SELECT DISTINCT product_category_name
FROM   olist_products
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Raw count of payments per category (ignoring payment type).
SELECT p.product_category_name,
       COUNT(*) AS num_payments
FROM   olist_order_items   AS oi
JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
JOIN   olist_products       AS p  ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
GROUP  BY p.product_category_name
ORDER  BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Payments per (category, payment_type) pair to see distribution.
SELECT p.product_category_name,
       op.payment_type,
       COUNT(*) AS num_payments
FROM   olist_order_items    AS oi
JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
JOIN   olist_products       AS p  ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
GROUP  BY p.product_category_name, op.payment_type
ORDER  BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Using a correlated sub‑query to pick the #1 payment type for every category.
SELECT t.product_category_name,
       t.payment_type,
       t.num_payments
FROM   (
        SELECT p.product_category_name      AS product_category_name,
               op.payment_type              AS payment_type,
               COUNT(*)                     AS num_payments
        FROM   olist_order_items    AS oi
        JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
        JOIN   olist_products       AS p  ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
        GROUP  BY p.product_category_name, op.payment_type
       ) AS t
WHERE  t.num_payments = (
        SELECT MAX(t2.num_payments)
        FROM   (
                SELECT COUNT(*) AS num_payments
                FROM   olist_order_items    AS oi2
                JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op2 ON op2.order_id = oi2.order_id
                JOIN   olist_products       AS p2  ON p2.product_id = oi2.product_id
                WHERE  p2.product_category_name = t.product_category_name
                GROUP  BY op2.payment_type
               ) AS t2
       )
ORDER BY t.num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Same idea but with a window function (ROW_NUMBER) – faster & clearer.
SELECT product_category_name,
       payment_type,
       num_payments
FROM   (
        SELECT p.product_category_name                AS product_category_name,
               op.payment_type                        AS payment_type,
               COUNT(*)                               AS num_payments,
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
                   PARTITION BY p.product_category_name
                   ORDER BY     COUNT(*) DESC
               ) AS rn
        FROM   olist_order_items    AS oi
        JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
        JOIN   olist_products       AS p  ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
        GROUP  BY p.product_category_name, op.payment_type
       )
WHERE  rn = 1
ORDER BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Add English translation for readability.
SELECT pct.product_category_name_english AS category_en,
       sub.payment_type,
       sub.num_payments
FROM   (
        SELECT p.product_category_name                AS product_category_name,
               op.payment_type                        AS payment_type,
               COUNT(*)                               AS num_payments,
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
                   PARTITION BY p.product_category_name
                   ORDER BY     COUNT(*) DESC
               ) AS rn
        FROM   olist_order_items    AS oi
        JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
        JOIN   olist_products       AS p  ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
        GROUP  BY p.product_category_name, op.payment_type
       ) AS sub
LEFT  JOIN product_category_name_translation AS pct
       ON pct.product_category_name = sub.product_category_name
WHERE  sub.rn = 1
ORDER  BY sub.num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final answer query – top‑3 categories whose MOST‑USED payment type
--                  has the greatest number of payments overall.
SELECT pct.product_category_name_english AS category_en,
       sub.payment_type,
       sub.num_payments
FROM   (
        SELECT p.product_category_name                AS product_category_name,
               op.payment_type                        AS payment_type,
               COUNT(*)                               AS num_payments,
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
                   PARTITION BY p.product_category_name
                   ORDER BY     COUNT(*) DESC
               ) AS rn
        FROM   olist_order_items    AS oi
        JOIN   olist_order_payments AS op ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
        JOIN   olist_products       AS p  ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
        GROUP  BY p.product_category_name, op.payment_type
       ) AS sub
LEFT  JOIN product_category_name_translation AS pct
       ON pct.product_category_name = sub.product_category_name
WHERE  sub.rn = 1                    -- keep only the MOST‑USED payment type per category
ORDER  BY sub.num_payments DESC      -- now sort by the size of that top payment type
LIMIT 3;                             -- …and show the TOP 3 categories
```

These ten queries take you from a simple inspection of available payment types all the way up to the exact query that will return:

• the three product categories with the largest number of payments made via their own most‑popular payment type,  
• the name of that dominant payment type, and  
• the count of payments that were made using it.
